3841 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 3842 0 R/Alt(Plot of log luminosity in erg per second, from 39.5 to 42.9, against time since explosion, from 0 to 250 days. The red-supergiant curve without heating starts at about 42.4, stays nearly flat for about 50 days and then declines, faster and faster, to 40.8 at day 250. The blue-supergiant curve without heating is about thirty times fainter, starting at 40.9 and falling below 39.5 near day 235. The blue-supergiant curve with nickel heating rises from 40.9 to a broad peak at about 41.5 near day 125, where it crosses the dotted curve of the radioactive heating rate, and then stays slightly above it, declining slowly to 41.2 at day 250.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[89]/Pg 15764 0 R>>
endobj
